 "answer_text": "Found 1 organism taxon record for CFTR: Homo sapiens [2]. \n\nGene Identity and Function\n\nThe CFTR gene encodes a member of the ATP-binding cassette (ABC) transporter superfamily that functions as a chloride channel, unique among ABC transporters, and controls ion and water secretion and absorption in epithelial tissues [1]. \n\nThese annotations align with the gene summary's description of the protein's role in controlling ion and water movement across epithelial membranes [1]. \n\nOrganism taxon records found\n\nOrganismTaxon NCBITaxon:9606, name: Homo sapiens [2]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene symbol: CFTR [3]. Gene name: CFTR [7]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Molecular Structure of the Human CFTR Ion Channel [4]. Pubmed title: ECFS standards of care on CFTR-related disorders: Diagnostic criteria of CFTR dysfunction [9]. Pubmed title: ECFS standards of care on CFTR-related disorders: Updated diagnostic criteria [12]. Pubmed title: Molecular structures reveal synergistic rescue of \u0394508 CFTR by Trikafta modulators [15]. Pubmed title: In vitro modulator responsiveness of 655 CFTR variants found in people with cystic fibrosis [18]. \n\nClinvar records found\n\nClinvar title: NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.1209+1988_1392+2067inv [5]. Clinvar title: NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.1392+2072_1392+2074del [10]. Clinvar title: NM_000492.4:c.165-291_1585-8528delinsATTTATTCCAAGGGAATAATAAAATAAATAATAATAATA [13]. Clinvar title: NM_000492.4:c.2619+2288_2989-839delinsATTAATAATAATAAAT [16]. Clinvar title: NM_000492.4:c.(164+1_165-1)_(1584+1_1585-1)del [19]. \n\nOmim records found\n\nCYSTIC FIBROSIS TRANSMEMBRANE CONDUCTANCE REGULATOR [6]. CFTR [6]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: NPDT Evaluation in Children With CFTR and (PSC) [8]. Clinical trial name: Study of VX-809 in Cystic Fibrosis Subjects With the \u2206F508-CFTR Gene Mutation [11]. Clinical trial name: Detection of Cystic Fibrosis Transmembrane Conductance Regulator (CFTR) Activity 